Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Marcus-Aurelius.md` against the entity-gap packet and the research file. `FRESH EYES REVIEW (2026-08-27)` block appended at the bottom. No body edits made.

**The two biggest issues:**

1. **The family is a clause, and grief is absent entirely.** Faustina gets half a sentence in the bio spine; the seven-or-eight buried children are a statistic in a subordinate clause and never return. The page renders Marcus wholly through self-correction — after reading it you know what he feared and wanted, not what he mourned. The packet lists wife/children as fact queries the page must satisfy, and right now only the FAQ metadata does. Pinnable material exists (Book 1.17's gratitude that his children were "not stupid nor deformed," the Homer/leaves passage in Book 10, the Epictetus kiss-your-child line in Book 11), all needing verification against the Long text.

2. **The strongest counterevidence is silently converted into wing evidence.** The research file flags three challenges to the Type 1 read — the effusive letters, clemency warmer than the stereotype, and his repeated refusal to correct anyone but himself. The draft files all three under "Wing: 1w2" as *supporting* evidence, and then the counterargument section only argues against Types 5 and 6. The third is the real objection and deserves an honest paragraph.

Also flagged: the Lyon 177 persecution is in the research file and dropped from the draft, leaving the hardest skeptical reading unfaced; the Ariston quote appears five times and the Book 8 opener four; and the body is at 4,063 of 4,500 words, past the warn line — so anything added has to be paid for with the listed cuts.

Sources consulted for the grief gap: [Big Think](https://bigthink.com/thinking/marcus-aurelius/), [Psychology Today](https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/hide-and-seek/202204/how-to-cope-with-loss-and-bereavement-the-stoic-way)
